{"name":"Heirloom Pink","hex":"#dbd5d0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"heirloom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A valued possession that has been passed down through the generations.","An old crop variety that has been passed down through generations of farmers by seed saving and cultivation, in contrast to modern cultivars used in large-scale agriculture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heirloom"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heirloom","blocks":[{"text":"In popular usage, an heirloom is something that has been passed down for generations through family members. Examples are a family Bible, antiques, weapons or jewellery."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Soldier%27s_return.jpg/330px-Soldier%27s_return.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heirloom","wikidata":"Q16842191"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Watch%2C_pocket_%28AM_1985.79-2%29.jpg/500px-Watch%2C_pocket_%28AM_1985.